@barney-s Thanks for the suggestion sharing your experience with Chainsaw in kro. I have some initial reservations about adopting a declarative framework like Chainsaw at this stage. While I can see the appeal of a declarative approach for its simplicity, I'm a bit concerned about potential limitations as agent-sandbox matures and our testing requirements become more complex. 

Given that Chainsaw is still in alpha and is maintained outside of the Kubernetes project, I think it would be more prudent for us to stick with a Go-based testing framework for now. This will give us the flexibility to tailor our tests to our specific needs and to evolve our testing strategy as the project grows.

I'm also open to reevaluating Chainsaw in the future as it matures and as we gain a better understanding of our long-term testing needs.

